   "note": "Outlines read off the sheet's three views (tools/trace/at46/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. ATR's Airport Planning Manuals aren't published on its public site; this is ATR's own dimensioned drawing, drawn as an illustration, so its confidence is medium. The 42-600 is the same airframe as the 42-500 (ATR's 42-600 brochure prints the same figures). The front view is drawn 2.1% smaller than the side and was rendered to its scale; the plan, drawn turned, was turned level. It draws the propeller disc 1.8% smaller than its printed 3.93 m, which the shape keeps. Doors from the side view; their sides as the ATR 72's (photos, AT76's sources)."
